          "shortDescription": "Build decentralized applications, smart contracts, and innovative Web3 solutions in a 24-hour online hackathon.",
          "description": "Web3 Nexus 2026 is a 24-hour online hackathon organized by the Blockchain Club in collaboration with the Department of Computer Science. The event invites students to explore the future of decentralized technologies by building secure, scalable, and user-friendly Web3 applications.\n\nParticipants will work in teams to develop decentralized applications (DApps), smart contracts, decentralized finance (DeFi) platforms, NFT marketplaces, DAO solutions, and blockchain-based identity systems. Throughout the hackathon, industry mentors will conduct virtual mentoring sessions, technical workshops, and project reviews.\n\nProjects will be judged on innovation, technical implementation, scalability, security, user experience, and overall impact.\n\nChallenge Tracks\nDecentralized Applications (DApps)\nSmart Contracts\nDeFi Applications\nDAO Governance Tools\nNFT Platforms\nWeb3 Social Platforms\nDecentralized Identity\nOpen Innovation",
