          "shortDescription": "Design intuitive and visually stunning digital experiences by solving real-world user experience challenges in this UI/UX hackathon.",
          "description": "DesignSprint 2026 is an 8-hour UI/UX Design Hackathon organized by the Design Club in collaboration with the Department of Computer Science. The event brings together aspiring designers, creative thinkers, and product enthusiasts to solve real-world problems through user-centered design.\n\nParticipants will work individually or in teams to research users, create wireframes, design high-fidelity interfaces, and build interactive prototypes using Figma or other design tools. Projects will be evaluated based on creativity, usability, accessibility, and design thinking.\n\nChallenge Tracks\nMobile App UI/UX\nWeb Application Design\nFinTech Experience Design\nHealthcare Applications\nEdTech Platforms\nSmart Campus Solutions\nAI Product Interfaces\nAccessibility & Inclusive Design",
